---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { minimumPaymentPayoffSchedule } from "../../lib/calc/creditCard";

const title = "Credit Card Minimum Payment Formula (How it works)";
const description =
  "Understand how credit card minimum payments are calculated and why balances can take so long to pay off. Educational use only.";

const exampleBalance = 3500;
const exampleApr = 22.9;
const exampleMinPercent = 2;
const exampleMinDollars = 29;
const example = minimumPaymentPayoffSchedule({
  balance: exampleBalance,
  aprPercent: exampleApr,
  minPercent: exampleMinPercent,
  minDollars: exampleMinDollars,
  maxMonths: 360
});
const month1 = example.rows[0];
const month12 = example.rows.length >= 12 ? example.rows[11] : null;
const money0 = new Intl.NumberFormat("en-US", { style: "currency", currency: "USD", minimumFractionDigits: 0, maximumFractionDigits: 0 });
const money2 = new Intl.NumberFormat("en-US", { style: "currency", currency: "USD", minimumFractionDigits: 2, maximumFractionDigits: 2 });
const pct2 = new Intl.NumberFormat("en-US", { minimumFractionDigits: 2, maximumFractionDigits: 2 });

const lastUpdated = "2026-02-17";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/guides/credit-card-minimum-payment-formula" lastUpdated={lastUpdated} robots="noindex, follow">
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Minimum payment formula</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>How credit card minimum payments are calculated</h1>
    <p>
      Minimum payments are often a small percentage of your balance with a dollar floor. That makes payoff slow when
      interest is high. Use this guide to understand the formula and model it accurately.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/minimum-payment-payoff-calculator">Minimum payment payoff</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/calculators/credit-card-payoff-calculator">Credit card payoff calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/credit-cards">Credit cards topic</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Credit card inputs to verify</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Current balance, APR, and any promo end date.</li>
      <li>Minimum payment rule or fixed payment amount.</li>
      <li>Fees or new purchases that affect the balance.</li>
      <li>Statement cycle dates and posting timing.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Typical minimum payment rules</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Minimum = max(dollar floor, percent of balance).</li>
      <li>Some issuers add interest and fees to the formula.</li>
      <li>Rules can differ by issuer and can change over time.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Minimum payment formula (example)</h2>
    <pre style="margin:10px 0 0"><code>Minimum payment = max(% of balance, dollar floor)
Example: max(2% x $3,500, $29) = max($70, $29) = $70</code></pre>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">
      Some issuers add interest and fees on top of that base number, which makes the minimum higher than the simple % rule.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Why payoff can take so long</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      If the minimum is close to the monthly interest, principal reduction is tiny. That keeps the balance high and
      stretches payoff over many years.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Worked example (computed)</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      Example: {money0.format(exampleBalance)} balance at {pct2.format(exampleApr)}% APR with a {exampleMinPercent}% minimum and
      {money0.format(exampleMinDollars)} floor.
    </p>
    <div style="overflow:auto; margin-top:12px">
      <table class="table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Checkpoint</th>
            <th class="num">Payment</th>
            <th class="num">Interest</th>
            <th class="num">Principal</th>
            <th class="num">Ending balance</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Month 1</td>
            <td class="num">{money2.format(month1.payment)}</td>
            <td class="num">{money2.format(month1.interest)}</td>
            <td class="num">{money2.format(month1.principal)}</td>
            <td class="num">{money2.format(month1.endingBalance)}</td>
          </tr>
          {month12 && (
            <tr>
              <td>Month 12</td>
              <td class="num">{money2.format(month12.payment)}</td>
              <td class="num">{money2.format(month12.interest)}</td>
              <td class="num">{money2.format(month12.principal)}</td>
              <td class="num">{money2.format(month12.endingBalance)}</td>
            </tr>
          )}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">
      The minimum payment can decline as the balance drops, which slows payoff unless you keep paying a fixed amount above the minimum.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">How to model your card</h2>
    <ol class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Use your statement APR (not a promo headline rate).</li>
      <li>Find the minimum payment rule on your statement or card agreement.</li>
      <li>Enter the percent and dollar floor in the calculator.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision inputs</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Issuer minimum payment formula from the statement.</li>
      <li>APR after any promo period ends.</li>
      <li>Fee schedule that can raise the minimum.</li>
      <li>Monthly payment you can commit above the minimum.</li>
      <li>Target payoff month or year.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Using a guessed percent that does not match your issuer.</li>
      <li>Ignoring interest and fees that can be added to the minimum.</li>
      <li>Assuming minimums stay the same when balances change.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/minimum-payment-payoff-calculator">Minimum payment payoff</a></li>
        <li><a href="/calculators/credit-card-payoff-calculator">Credit card payoff calculator</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/why-minimum-payments-take-so-long">Why minimum payments take so long</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/how-credit-card-interest-is-calculated">How credit card interest is calculated</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Checklist: match your issuer</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Check whether interest and fees are added to the minimum.</li>
      <li>Confirm the dollar floor (often $25 or $35).</li>
      <li>Verify the percent-of-balance rule in the cardmember agreement.</li>
      <li>Re-check after promo periods end.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">FAQ</h2>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Can issuers change the minimum rule?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Yes. Issuers can update the formula, so check statements or account terms periodically.
    </p>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Does paying more than the minimum help a lot?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Usually yes. Even a small extra amount can reduce total interest and shorten payoff time.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/minimum-payment-payoff-calculator">Run the minimum payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/calculators/credit-card-payoff-calculator">Compare a fixed payment</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/credit-cards">Credit cards topic</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-02-17</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>





